  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23958931"
    description: "Concept DOI on Zenodo -- always resolves to the latest version"
abstract: >-
  OmniOmics is a desktop application that packages five Snakemake workflows for
  metagenomics (MAGMA), isolate genomics (SIGMA), metatranscriptomics (DOGMA),
  differential expression (DEFINE) and amplicon metabarcoding (PRISM) behind a
  graphical interface, together with an integrated plotting environment that
  turns each workflow's output into publication-ready figures. The same runs
  can be started from a command line, on a server or as one job on a PBS
  cluster. Each pipeline was validated end to end on a public, non-simulated
  dataset with a published expected result; the configurations, reference
  data and results are published at github.com/oliv-angelus/OmniOmics-validation
  and reported in the accompanying manuscript.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - metagenomics
  - metatranscriptomics
  - amplicon sequencing
  - Snakemake
  - reproducibility
